KJV renders: extortioner.

H4161.strongs:
Origin: or מֹצָאxlit môtsâ corrected to môtsâʼ; from 3318;
Meaning: a going forth, i.e. (the act) an egress, or (the place) an exit; hence, a source or product; specifically, dawn, the rising of the sun (the East), exportation, utterance, a gate, a fountain, a mine, a meadow (as producing grass)
KJV renders: brought out, bud, that which came out, east, going forth, goings out, that which (thing that) is gone out, outgoing, proceeded out, spring, vein, (water-) course (springs).

H4162.strongs:
Origin: the same as 4161;
Meaning: Motsa, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Moza.

H4164.strongs:
Origin: or מוּצָק; from 3332;
Meaning: narrowness; figuratively, distress
KJV renders: anguish, is straitened, straitness.

H4165.strongs:
Origin: from 5694;
Meaning: properly, fusion, i.e. literally, a casting (of metal); figuratively, a mass (of clay)
KJV renders: casting, hardness.

H4166.strongs:
Origin: or מֻצָקָה; from 3332;
Meaning: properly, something poured out, i.e. a casting (of metal); by implication, a tube (as cast)
KJV renders: when it was cast, pipe.

H4167.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to jeer, i.e. (intens.) blaspheme
KJV renders: be corrupt.

H4168.strongs:
Origin: from 3344;
Meaning: a fire or fuel; abstractly, a conflagration
KJV renders: burning, hearth.

H4169.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 4168;
Meaning: fuel
KJV renders: burning.

H4170.strongs:
Origin: or מֹקֵשׁ; from 3369;
Meaning: a noose (for catching animals) (literally or figuratively); by implication, a hook (for the nose)
KJV renders: be ensnared, gin, (is) snare(-d), trap.

H4171.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to alter; by implication, to barter, to dispose of
KJV renders: × at all, (ex-) change, remove.

H4172.strongs:
Origin: or מֹרָא; or מוֹרָהxlit môrâh corrected to môwrâh; (Psalm 9:20), from 3372;
Meaning: fear; by implication, a fearful thing or deed
KJV renders: dread, (that ought to be) fear(-ed), terribleness, terror.

H4173.strongs:
Origin: or מֹרַג; from an unused root meaning to triturate;
Meaning: a threshing sledge
KJV renders: threshing instrument.

H4174.strongs:
Origin: from 3381;
Meaning: a descent; as architecture, an ornamental appendage, perhaps a festoon
KJV renders: going down, steep place, thin work.

H4176.strongs:
Origin: or מֹרֶה; the same as 4175;
Meaning: Moreh, a Canaanite; also a hill (perhaps named from him)
KJV renders: Moreh.

H4177.strongs:
Origin: from 4171 in the sense of shearing;
Meaning: a razor
KJV renders: razor.

H4178.strongs:
Origin: from 3399;
Meaning: obstinate, i.e. independent
KJV renders: peeled.

H4179.strongs:
Origin: or מֹרִיָּה; from 7200 and 3050; seen of Jah;
Meaning: Morijah, a hill in Palestine
KJV renders: Moriah.

H4180.strongs:
Origin: from 3423;
Meaning: a possession; figuratively, delight
KJV renders: possession, thought.

H4181.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 4180;
Meaning: a possession
KJV renders: heritage, inheritance, possession.

H4182.strongs:
Origin: from 3423 and 1661; possession of Gath;
Meaning: Moresheth-Gath, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Moresheth-gath.

H4183.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 4182;
Meaning: a Morashtite or inhabitant of Moresheth-Gath
KJV renders: Morashthite.

H4184.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to touch
KJV renders: feel, handle.

H4185.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as 4184 through the idea of receding by contact);
Meaning: to withdraw (both literally and figuratively, whether intransitive or transitive)
KJV renders: cease, depart, go back, remove, take away.

H4186.strongs:
Origin: or מֹשָׁב; from 3427;
Meaning: a seat; figuratively, a site; abstractly, a session; by extension an abode (the place or the time); by implication, population
KJV renders: assembly, dwell in, dwelling(-place), wherein (that) dwelt (in), inhabited place, seat, sitting, situation, sojourning.

H4187.strongs:
Origin: or מֻשִּׁי; from 4184; sensitive;
Meaning: Mushi, a Levite
KJV renders: Mushi.

H4188.strongs:
Origin: patronymical from 4187;
Meaning: a Mushite (collectively) or descendants of Mushi
KJV renders: Mushites.

H4189.strongs:
Origin: act participle feminine of 4900;
Meaning: something drawing, i.e. (figuratively) a cord
KJV renders: band.

H4190.strongs:
Origin: from 3467;
Meaning: deliverance
KJV renders: salvation.

H4191.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to die (literally or figuratively); causatively, to kill
KJV renders: × at all, × crying, (be) dead (body, man, one), (put to, worthy of) death, destroy(-er), (cause to, be like to, must) die, kill, necro(-mancer), × must needs, slay, × surely, × very suddenly, × in (no) wise.

H4192.strongs:
Origin: (Psalm 48:14) or מוּת לַבֵּן; from 4191 and 1121 with the preposition and article interposed;
Meaning: 'To die for the son', probably the title of a popular song
KJV renders: death, Muthlabben.

H4193.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 4194;
Meaning: death
KJV renders: death.

H4194.strongs:
Origin: from 4191;
Meaning: death (natural or violent); concretely, the dead, their place or state (hades); figuratively, pestilence, ruin
KJV renders: (be) dead(-ly), death, die(-d).

H4195.strongs:
Origin: from 3498;
Meaning: literally gain; figuratively, superiority
KJV renders: plenteousness, preeminence, profit.

H4196.strongs:
Origin: from 2076;
Meaning: an altar
KJV renders: altar.

H4197.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to mingle (water with wine);
Meaning: tempered wine
KJV renders: liquor.

H4198.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to suck out;
Meaning: exhausted
KJV renders: burnt.

H4199.strongs:
Origin: probably from an unused root meaning to faint with fear; terror;
Meaning: Mizzah, an Edomite
KJV renders: Mizzah.
